    feat(promotion): wire the separate reviewer identity into /promote auto-merge
    
    Closes the gap where /promote promised separate-identity auto-approval but used the
    ambient gh identity (so it always self-approval-failed to HUMAN). Now:
    
    - promotion.reviewer.tokenEnv (schema + seeded config) names the env var holding the
      approver token; /promote reads it and runs approve+merge with GH_TOKEN scoped to
      only those two calls, and checks the reviewer login != PR author.
    - Get-PromotionDecision/promotion_decision take a ReviewerConfigured bool (PS 8th
      param / bash $8), fail-closed $false: a LOW change with every other gate green still
      goes HUMAN when no separate reviewer is configured. The fail-closed decision lives in
      tested code, not prose.
    - docs/promotion.md §3 rewritten to the as-built (config key, setup, repo auto-merge +
      classifier allowlist notes); harness-doctor check 11(g); plugin 0.2.10 -> 0.2.11.
    - +5 twin assertions each (PS 239/0, bash 229/0), mutation-verified: neutering the gate
      reddens exactly the reviewer assertions on both runners.
    
