Conclusion: the same PR that James-Lloyd could NOT self-approve was approved by the
separate write identity jl-pr-reviewer. The precondition in docs/promotion.md §3 holds:
a second write identity is both necessary (self-approval rejected) and sufficient
(second-identity approval accepted) for the auto-approve step. Promotion remains
enabled:false — this establishes only the identity half of S3.

