115:### 7. Write the audit record BEFORE acting
116:Every automated approval must be attributable after the fact, so the record is written whether the
117:outcome is AUTO or HUMAN, and it is written *first* (before §8 acts).
118:
119:Write `state/evidence/<task-id>/risk.json`:
120:```json
121:{ "range": "<BASE>..<HEAD>", "environment": "staging|prod",
122:  "deterministicTier": "LOW|MEDIUM|HIGH", "deterministicReasons": ["..."],
123:  "classifierTier": "LOW|MEDIUM|HIGH", "classifierProof": "<its escalation lines, verbatim>",
124:  "finalTier": "LOW|MEDIUM|HIGH",
125:  "preconditions": { "gateGreen": true, "reviewShip": true, "e2eEvidence": true },
126:  "reviewerConfigured": true, "reviewerIdentity": "<the reviewer login, never its token>",
127:  "decision": "AUTO|HUMAN", "reason": "<the decision function's reason string>",
128:  "changedFiles": ["..."], "changedLines": 0 }
129:```
130:Then append one line to the current run's `harness/.runs/<runId>/ledger.jsonl` (newest run dir; if
131:there is no run in progress, create `harness/.runs/promote-$(date +%Y%m%dT%H%M%S)/`):
132:```json
133:{"iter":0,"result":"risk","tier":"LOW","decision":"AUTO","env":"staging","path":"claude","usedFallback":false}
134:```
135:
136:### 8. Act
137:**On `AUTO`** (only ever reachable for staging + LOW + all preconditions met + `promotion.enabled` +
138:a resolved separate reviewer identity):
139:1. Post a structured comment on the PR, criterion by criterion — each check, whether it passed, and
140:   why (name the reviewer identity, never its token). A bare "approved by automation" is not an audit
141:   trail.
142:2. Approve and merge **as the reviewer identity**, scoping its token to only these two calls:
143:   `GH_TOKEN=$tok gh pr review <n> --approve` then `GH_TOKEN=$tok gh pr merge <n> --auto --squash`.
144:   **Re-read the token from its env var in the SAME shell invocation as these two calls** — shell
145:   state does not survive between separate command runs, so a `$tok` captured back in §6 is empty
146:   here and the approve would silently run unauthenticated. If the approve call does not succeed,
147:   STOP — take the HUMAN path and never run the merge. (`--auto` also requires the repo's "Allow
148:   auto-merge" setting to be on; if merge reports it is disabled, say so and leave the PR approved
149:   for a human to merge.)
150:
151:**On `HUMAN`** (everything else):
152:1. Post the same structured comment, headed **ESCALATED**, naming exactly which criteria tripped or
153:   which precondition was unmet (including *reviewer identity not configured / equals author* when
154:   that was the cause).
155:2. Label the PR `risk:medium` / `risk:high`, plus `needs-human`.
156:3. Append to `state/handoff.md` under `## Needs human decision`, with the range and the reasons.
157:4. **Do not merge. Do not approve.** Not even "it's obviously fine" — that judgement is the thing
158:   this command exists to remove.
159:
160:### 9. Probe failures are HUMAN, not merge
161:Before any `gh` call (including the §6 identity resolution), probe: `gh --version`, `gh auth status`,
162:and that a PR exists for this branch (`gh pr view --json number`). Any failure ⇒ the HUMAN path,
163:saying which probe failed.
164:
165:**GitHub rejects self-approval.** §6 pre-empts this by requiring the reviewer login to differ from the
166:author before AUTO is even possible. If a self-approval rejection still surfaces at approve time
167:(e.g. the env var was pointed at the author's own token), treat it as HUMAN and say so plainly; never
168:fall through to `gh pr merge` on an approval that did not land.
