- `plugin/commands/promote.md:32` — blocker — The decision is not bound to the PR actually merged. It classifies local `BASE..HEAD` against `main`, then only checks that some PR exists; it never verifies `headRefOid == HEAD` or that `baseRefName` equals `promotion.staging.branch`. `/promote staging` can therefore classify one range and merge a newer/different PR—or a PR targeting `main`, bypassing “prod is never automated.” Resolve the PR first, validate its head and configured target branch, and classify that exact PR range; pin these checks in tests.

- `plugin/commands/promote.md:115` — blocker — `risk.json` and the ledger record `decision: AUTO` before approval/merge, but lines 146–149 turn approval or merge failures into HUMAN without finalizing either record. The durable audit can therefore falsely report AUTO and omit the actual failure, violating the attributable-audit contract. Record pre-action intent separately, then always append/finalize the actual approval and merge outcome with its failure reason.

- `docs/promotion.md:59` — blocker — GitHub App installation tokens are advertised as supported, but `plugin/commands/promote.md:100` identifies the reviewer through `GET /user`. GitHub documents that endpoint for GitHub App user access tokens and PATs, not installation access tokens, so the advertised App path always fails closed and is unusable. [GitHub endpoint documentation](https://docs.github.com/en/rest/users/users?apiVersion=2022-11-28#get-the-authenticated-user). Remove that claim or implement and test an installation-token-specific identity/action path.

- `state/evidence/2026-08-13-s3-reviewer-identity/README.md:16` — blocker — The evidence predates this batch and only demonstrates manual `gh auth switch` plus raw approval. It does not exercise `reviewer.tokenEnv`, scoped `GH_TOKEN`, identity comparison, the decision call, audit output, or conditional merge. This violates the project requirement that every change carry end-to-end evidence. Run the integrated `/promote` path against a controlled real PR and capture sanitized success and failure artifacts.

VERDICT: REJECT
